---
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
const fig = (name) => `${base.replace(/\/$/, '')}/figures/${name}`;
---
<div class="evlearn-root">
  <div class="evlearn-kicker">VISUAL FOUNDATION · PIXEL ELECTRONICS · EVENT MODELS</div>
  <h2>From photons to asynchronous events</h2>
  <p class="evlearn-lead">Follow one changing pixel from the optical image through its analog front-end, reference comparator, ON/OFF trigger and timestamped output. This is a functional circuit abstraction, not a transistor-level schematic.</p>
  <div class="evlearn-flow">
    <div class="evlearn-step"><span>01 / INPUT</span><strong>Incident light</strong><small>Moving edge causes a change in local irradiance</small><div class="evlearn-mini-scene"><span class="evlearn-disc"></span><span class="evlearn-pixel"></span></div></div>
    <div class="evlearn-step"><span>02 / ANALOG</span><strong>Photoreceptor + log</strong><small>Photocurrent converted to log-domain electrical signal</small><div class="evlearn-formula">L(t) = log I(t)</div></div>
    <div class="evlearn-step"><span>03 / DIFFERENCE</span><strong>Change detector</strong><small>Current brightness is compared with the last reference</small><div class="evlearn-formula">ΔL = L − L<sub>ref</sub></div></div>
    <div class="evlearn-step"><span>04 / THRESHOLD</span><strong>ON / OFF comparator</strong><small>Threshold crossing generates a polarity event</small><div class="evlearn-polarity"><b>+ ON</b><b>− OFF</b></div></div>
    <div class="evlearn-step"><span>05 / OUTPUT</span><strong>Event + reference update</strong><small>Pixel address, timestamp and polarity are reported</small><div class="evlearn-formula">e = (x, y, t, p)</div></div>
  </div>
  <div class="evlearn-two">
    <article class="evlearn-card"><h3>DAVIS: two sensing paths</h3><p>In a DAVIS pixel, the photodiode is shared. The <b class="evlearn-blue">APS path</b> supports conventional intensity frames, whereas the <b class="evlearn-orange">DVS path</b> reacts to temporal contrast and emits events.</p><div class="evlearn-path"><div>Shared photodiode</div><div class="evlearn-pathways"><span>APS → frame readout</span><span>DVS → ΔL → comparator → event</span></div></div></article>
    <article class="evlearn-card"><h3>Idealized temporal contrast</h3><p>The voltage-level change is modeled as a log-brightness difference relative to a stored reference. Both the threshold and reference are pixel-local.</p><svg viewBox="0 0 500 178" role="img" aria-label="Illustrative brightness curve and ON OFF events" width="100%"><path d="M34 15V143H486" stroke="#8797ae" fill="none" opacity=".7"/><path d="M35 107 C105 107 116 49 169 47 S233 103 283 95 S360 132 480 130" stroke="#44d4fa" stroke-width="3" fill="none"/><path d="M34 64H486 M34 114H486" stroke="#90acc5" stroke-dasharray="5 6" opacity=".35"/><circle cx="153" cy="53" r="6" fill="#38c8f0"/><circle cx="344" cy="119" r="6" fill="#ff987b"/><text x="145" y="28" fill="#38c8f0" font-size="13">ON</text><text x="339" y="154" fill="#ff987b" font-size="13">OFF</text><text x="44" y="174" fill="#b7cce1" font-size="12">time →</text></svg></article>
  </div>
  <h2>Complete five-stage concept map</h2>
  <p>The figure brings together the conventional image, the simplified DAVIS circuit, the mathematical event rule, a functional neuromorphic analogy, and the resulting event-image/voxel-grid representations.</p>
  <figure class="evlearn-figure"><img src={fig('from-light-to-asynchronous-events.png')} alt="Detailed five-column infographic: conventional image, DAVIS pixel electronics, mathematical model, retina-inspired change sensing, event image and voxel-grid output" loading="lazy"/><figcaption>Figure A. Conceptual event-generation chain. The retina comparison is an analogy, not a claim that silicon pixels contain biological neurons. <a href={fig('from-light-to-asynchronous-events.png')} target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open full-size illustration ↗</a></figcaption></figure>
  <div class="evlearn-note"><strong>Technical distinction</strong><span>The ON/OFF thresholds act on a difference relative to the event-updated reference, not directly on fixed absolute values of L(t). Real circuits have finite bandwidth, noise, refractory effects, and ON/OFF asymmetry.</span></div>
  <h2>Sensor architecture and representations</h2>
  <div class="evlearn-three"><article class="evlearn-card"><span class="evlearn-index">A</span><h3>Intensity frames vs events</h3><p>Frames sample scene intensity on a schedule. Events communicate threshold-crossing changes at independent pixels.</p></article><article class="evlearn-card"><span class="evlearn-index">B</span><h3>High temporal resolution</h3><p>Fine timestamps describe *when* changes occurred. Timestamp precision is not the same as latency or maximum per-pixel event rate.</p></article><article class="evlearn-card"><span class="evlearn-index">C</span><h3>Event representations</h3><p>Accumulated image: spatial counts. Voxel grid: temporal bins. Time surface: recency of the last event per pixel.</p></article></div>
  <figure class="evlearn-figure evlearn-tall"><img src={fig('how-event-cameras-work-infographic.png')} alt="Long-form visual overview of how event cameras work, event sensor categories, DAVIS pixel architecture and event representations" loading="lazy"/><figcaption>Figure B. Long-form illustrated roadmap. Detailed descriptions and equations remain selectable text in the lesson; image is a visual aid. <a href={fig('how-event-cameras-work-infographic.png')} target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open full-size roadmap ↗</a></figcaption></figure>
</div>
<style>
.evlearn-root{--ec:#3bcdf5;color:var(--sl-color-text);margin:2rem 0 3rem}.evlearn-root *{box-sizing:border-box}.evlearn-root h2{font-size:clamp(1.35rem,2.4vw,2rem);line-height:1.2;margin:2.1rem 0 .65rem}.evlearn-root h3{font-size:1.04rem;margin:0 0 .55rem}.evlearn-root p{line-height:1.68;margin:0 0 1.15rem}.evlearn-kicker{font-size:.73rem;font-weight:800;letter-spacing:.13em;color:var(--ec)}.evlearn-lead{max-width:75ch;color:var(--sl-color-gray-2)}.evlearn-flow{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(5,minmax(0,1fr));gap:.6rem;margin:1.4rem 0}.evlearn-step,.evlearn-card{background:#0e1d33;border:1px solid #294867;border-radius:13px;padding:1rem;color:#e6f2ff}.evlearn-step{min-height:205px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:.65rem}.evlearn-step>span,.evlearn-index{color:var(--ec);font-size:.68rem;font-weight:800;letter-spacing:.08em}.evlearn-step strong{font-size:.95rem;line-height:1.3}.evlearn-step small{color:#a9bdd2;font-size:.75rem;line-height:1.55}.evlearn-formula{margin-top:auto;font-size:.86rem;color:#a7edff;background:#142c46;border-radius:7px;padding:.55rem;text-align:center}.evlearn-mini-scene{margin-top:auto;height:46px;background:linear-gradient(100deg,#09121d,#1a2737);border-radius:7px;position:relative;overflow:hidden}.evlearn-disc{position:absolute;width:26px;height:26px;border-radius:50%;background:#eee;left:38%;top:10px;box-shadow:-18px 0 10px #8ca1b266,-32px 0 10px #8ca1b233}.evlearn-pixel{position:absolute;border:2px solid #39d1ed;width:8px;height:8px;left:48%;top:18px}.evlearn-polarity{display:flex;gap:.3rem;margin-top:auto}.evlearn-polarity b{flex:1;background:#123954;border-radius:6px;text-align:center;color:#4bd8fe;font-size:.73rem;padding:.5rem .1rem}.evlearn-polarity b+ b{background:#422a31;color:#ff9f84}.evlearn-two,.evlearn-three{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr));gap:.8rem;margin:1.25rem 0}.evlearn-three{grid-template-columns:repeat(3,minmax(0,1fr))}.evlearn-card p{color:#b9cbdf;font-size:.88rem;margin:0}.evlearn-blue{color:#59cffb}.evlearn-orange{color:#ff9d85}.evlearn-path{margin-top:.8rem;display:flex;gap:1rem;align-items:center;font-size:.76rem}.evlearn-path>div:first-child{padding:.6rem;border:1px solid #5daacb;border-radius:6px}.evlearn-pathways{display:grid;gap:.4rem}.evlearn-pathways span{border:1px solid #4b7eaa;border-radius:5px;padding:.5rem;color:#a8e7fe}.evlearn-pathways span+span{border-color:#c3765f;color:#ffc4b0}.evlearn-figure{margin:1.2rem 0;background:#071628;border:1px solid #1e6384;border-radius:12px;overflow:hidden}.evlearn-figure img{display:block;width:100%;height:auto}.evlearn-figure figcaption{padding:.8rem 1rem;background:#102338;color:#b8cee1;font-size:.78rem;line-height:1.6}.evlearn-figure a{color:#65d9ff}.evlearn-note{display:flex;gap:1.2rem;padding:1rem;border-left:3px solid #39d2f4;background:#11253b;border-radius:7px;font-size:.87rem;margin-top:1rem}.evlearn-note strong{color:#68daf8;min-width:115px}.evlearn-note span{color:#d1e2f3}.evlearn-index{display:inline-block;margin-bottom:.5rem}
@media(max-width:1000px){.evlearn-flow{grid-template-columns:repeat(3,minmax(0,1fr))}}@media(max-width:670px){.evlearn-flow,.evlearn-two,.evlearn-three{grid-template-columns:1fr}.evlearn-step{min-height:unset}.evlearn-note{flex-direction:column;gap:.4rem}}
</style>
